    {
     "type": "code",
     "head": "Earliest end in code",
     "say": "Here it is. Each meeting is stored as end, then start, so sort puts the earliest end first. Count and last start empty. If a meeting starts at or after last, take it and move last to its end. Sorting costs O of n log n, the loop is linear. Our five meetings print three.",
     "panels": [
      {
       "file": "sol.cpp",
       "code": "int maxMeetings(vector<pair<int, int>> a) {\n    sort(a.begin(), a.end());\n    int cnt = 0, last = INT_MIN;\n    for (auto& [e, s] : a)\n        if (s >= last) { cnt++; last = e; }\n    return cnt;\n}\nint main() { cout << maxMeetings({{4,1},{5,3},{6,0},{7,5},{9,8}}); }"
      }
     ],
     "steps": [
